From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:47:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): preserve quota scope and inert recovery evidence
 [daveey]

Review reproduced a per-model live quota reset widened to its entire provider, and common text ingress treating historical mandates as current policy. Existing tests covered distinct providers and direct positive restrictions, not healthy same-provider siblings or real escalation of legacy titles.

Keep provider-wide walls separate from model probes. Forward legacy directives as labelled JSON evidence with trailing active text still validated; allow bounded past-tense configuration observations, not new mandates. Preserve original author/source rows, reserve and no-claim gates. Correct audit-only model attribution guidance.

Proof: unchanged independent probes reproduced 0 pass / 3 fail; expanded dispatch/provider-wall/order/history/refusal regressions plus text/transport consumers 37 passed, retries off. Importing and facade consumer sweep retained in consumers33-valid.log. Full scripts/check required before publication; exact-head CI and independent review remain mandatory.
